alex.s: FYI customer opened an escalation — duplicate POSTs causing billing spikes + intermittent 502s. They say our client retried and the server processed twice. Request IDs in logs: r-8f3a, r-8f3a (same id, two completions). https://support.redwood.ai/tickets/INC-1234
priya.k: ugh. Which SDK & node version? Any repro snippet from them?
mike: customer reported using node 20 + ts-sdk 0.9.2 with a small custom retry wrapper around global fetch. They mention reusing an AbortController across retries.
alex.s: here's the minimal repro they pasted (redacted):
```js
// bad: reusing controller across retries
const ac = new AbortController();
async function send(body) {
  try {
    return await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/outputs', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'authorization': `Bearer ${token}` },
      body: JSON.stringify(body),
      signal: ac.signal
    });
  } catch (e) {
    // retry after backoff but reuse 'ac' -> signal already aborted or timed out
    await sleep(200);
    return fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/outputs', { method:'POST', body: JSON.stringify(body), signal: ac.signal });
  }
}
```
priya.k: that stands out. Reusing AbortController can leave signal in aborted state or hold on to timers depending on undici/global fetch interplay. Also if they use undici pool options combined with retries we can get duplicate sends when the body stream/clone behavior mismatches.
tara: Do we have logs correlating r-8f3a to two different server side receipts? I can grep traces.
infra-bot: Found two completion events for r-8f3a: completed @ 2026-02-14T21:12:03Z (200), completed @ 2026-02-14T21:12:05Z (200). Both processed.
priya.k: timeline suggests client retried after a transient timeout, server processed both. Need repro that demonstrates AbortSignal reuse + backoff jitter missing.
alex.s: customer also included Node undici debug dump:
```
undici: pool socket destroyed before body drained
undici: request aborted by signal
```

mike: common guidance: create a fresh AbortController per attempt, ensure any stream bodies are cloneable or recreated per retry. Also add jitter to avoid synchronized retries.
priya.k: I pushed a short patch for our example app in docs showing safe retry pattern. Patch snippet: 
```js
async function postWithRetries(url, body, token) {
  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
    const ac = new AbortController(); // new per attempt
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'authorization': `Bearer ${token}`, 'content-type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(body),
        signal: ac.signal
      });
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`status:${res.status}`);
      return res.json();
    } catch (err) {
      ac.abort();
      const backoff = 100 * Math.pow(2, i) + Math.floor(Math.random() * 200); // jitter
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff));
    }
  }
  throw new Error('exhausted retries');
}
```
tara: also recommend avoiding reusing ReadableStream bodies; use string/Buffer payloads or recreate stream each retry. Add idempotency-key header on customer side for POSTs that mutate billing/accounting.
priya.k: opened internal ticket to update docs + add SDK example to 0.9.x migration guide. Link: https://go.redwood.ai/issue/SDK-RETRY-452
alex.s: customer notified with recommended workaround (idempotency-key + fresh AbortController). They applied a short patch and reported no duplicates in 24h.
support-bot: Customer INC-1234 updated: asked to validate with canary traffic for 48h, assigned to support-eng.
mike: side note — if they use undici's body streaming with FormData, ensure to call formData.stream() per attempt (not reuse underlying stream).
priya.k: leaving a quick checklist for support engineers handling similar escalations:
• ask SDK + node version
• ask for client retry code, specifically AbortController usage
• confirm whether payload stream/Buffer is reused
• recommend idempotency-key for mutating POSTs
• suggest fresh AbortController per try + exponential backoff with jitter
• if using undici, try upgrade to latest compatible version (fixes some signal/timer edge cases)

alex.s: thanks all. I'll close the loop with the customer and attach the doc patch. :thumbsup:
